the chances of mark ruffalo getting a  solo Hulk movie seem like they're slim  to none but the Hulk's been one of the  most visible superhero movie stars for  decades here's a look back at all the  Hulk movies ranked from worst to best  the last of three Incredible Hulk  revival TV movies was the death of the  Incredible Hulk  but despite the title and its status as  the final chapter banners death wasn't  meant to be permanent there was meant to  be a follow-up called The Revenge of the  Incredible Hulk but it never happened  possibly due to star Bill Bixby failing  health but more likely because death of  the Incredible Hulk got abysmally low  ratings the good news is that this meant  very few people got to see the moronic  manner of the Hulk's death he falls from  an airplane seriously that's it if  you're a fan of both the comics and the  show you learned a long time ago to  accept that TVs Hulk wasn't even close  to the comics version in terms of power  still the whole dying from a long fall  would be like Logan ending with  Wolverine dying from the flu part of the  goal of the late 80s Incredible Hulk  revival was to use a familiar face to  introduce some of the other Marvel  franchises to audiences that's why trial  of the Incredible Hulk was the debut of  the first live-action Matt Murdock aka  daredevil who represents banner after he  witnesses a crime linked to the kingpin  while daredevil fans likely wouldn't put  trial of The Incredible Hulk  any higher on a list than Hulk fans  would the movie gives way more attention  to the Man Without Fear than the green  Goliath while he makes a ruckus earlier  in the movie banners gigantic alter ego  doesn't even get close to the climactic  action during the final fight instead  pretty much everything is in the hands  of Daredevils badly choreographed  martial arts angley's Hulk is not well  loved but maybe it deserves a break at  the very least it was trying to be more  than just another popcorn action flick  the script isn't great and most of the  performances are wooden the story is  often boring with Lee waiting a long  time to introduce the Hulk and waiting  even longer for the film's only  impressive action scenes Hulk's battle  in the desert with the military the  effects are inconsistent with some shots  coming off as stunning and others are  embarrassingly cartoonish that said  there's a lot of mythic imagery Lee  connects the Hulk with nature which is  why he  works and moments with the Hulk  mesmerized by certain rock formations  and why it almost makes sense that one  of the most memorable fights in the film  comes when the Hulk takes on a bunch of  gamma-powered Hulk dogs almost Lee tried  to make something unique in entertaining  he thoroughly fails at the ladder but  you have to admit that he went for it  in 1988 American network television got  its first new installment of david  banners lonely saga since 1982 in the  made-for-tv movie The Incredible Hulk  returns along with Bill Bixby and Lou  Ferrigno return stars Eric Alan Kramer  as Thor and Steve Levitt as the Thunder  gods classic alter-ego Donald Blake it's  definitely pretty far from perfect but  of the three TV movies returns is by far  the most bearable unlike death The Hulk  doesn't die in a ridiculous way  and unlike trial the guest superhero  actually adds to the plot instead of  completely stealing the show Hulk and  Thor have their compulsory battle in a  lab almost 25 years before Chris  Hemsworth and Mark Ruffalo would tussle  on the deck of a Helicarrier or Duke it  out in an outerspace gladiatorial arena  admittedly their eventual team-up later  in the film feels way more like a fight  from an episode of the a-team than an  epic clash of strength between the  strongest Avengers but the fight is  still absolutely worth watching if  nothing else you can see how far we've  come since 1988 if this were a different  kind of ranked movie list there's a  really good chance of vengers infinity  war would make it a lot closer to the  top but as a Hulk movie it doesn't have  much to offer after that first opening  scene on the refugee ship the Hulk  pretty much disappears we see a few  flashes of green when Bruce Banner tries  and fails to get the other guy to come  out and it even has a couple of good  banner moments  [Music]  that's about it though and even worse  the Hulk totally gets warped if you're  not familiar with the Worf effect the  name refers to how often the  enterprise's Klingon security chief gets  beat up on Star Trek The Next Generation  it's an easy trope the bad guy beats up  the biggest baddest good guy early in  the story so the audience knows he's a  threat  The Hulk getting trounced and the nearly  vanishing would each be bad enough on  their own but together we eventually got  some good character development out of  it but for Hulk fans it adds up to some  surprising disappointment - infinity war  oh we got a lot to figure out pal  Incredible Hulk is probably not on the  top of anyone's list of MCU films but  the truth is it's probably a whole lot  better than you remember at the very  least it's not bad for one thing it  introduces the green Guide much sooner  than its 2003 predecessor for another it  gives us a lot more action in the form  of one classic Hulk villain the  abomination and the foundation for the  emergence of another in the form of dr.  Samuel Sterns a named Hulk fans would  recognize belonging to the master mind  villain the leader  it even has Stan Lee turning into a Hulk  and even if that happens off screen it's  definitely fun to think about plus it  stands to reason that Edie Norton could  have been the perfect Bruce Banner he  built his career playing characters who  were meek pushovers one second and  intimidating bullies the next  unfortunately his talents aren't really  used well in what amounts to a formulaic  action flick with no real glimpse of who  Bruce Banner is the CGI rendering of the  Hulk is definitely more consistent than  what we saw in angley's Hulk and the  monsters bellowing roar is a huge  improvement but watching Incredible Hulk  now the effects look primitive compared  to what we see in everything that comes  after for a Hulk fan age of Ultron was a  tough pill to swallow for the sake of  the plot Ironman needs to win their mid  movie tussle and as cool as it is to see  the Hulkbuster armor in action it raises  the question of why they even need the  Hulk around if Tony Stark can just build  something stronger whenever he wants it  does have some bright spots though  regardless of who wins the Hulk Iron Man  battle is wonderfully executed and in  the final conflict hoax probably the  only Avenger to successfully use his  teeth to trash robots  takes out Ultron in one shot twice there  are also some wonderful character  moments for Hulk an age of Ultron  whether you like the romances Black  Widow or not it reveals an interesting  side of banner we haven't seen before  while most of this list is for live  action flicks 2010's Planet Hulk is a  worthy exception based on the comic  storyline of the same name Planet Hulk  is about the green Goliath being exiled  by Earth's other heroes to the planet  Sekar where he becomes a gladiator and  eventually leads a revolt against the  tyrannical Red King Planet Hulk was  about as faithful to its source material  as a comic book movie could get stuff is  left out for time with the final battle  between Hulk and the Red King playing  out a little differently and the Holts  major gladiatorial battle is against  Thor's spacefaring buddy beta ray bill  instead of the Silver Surfer the biggest  change though is that it stops short of  the cataclysmic explosion that the comic  story ends with in the comics that acted  as a prologue to hold returning to Earth  for payback in the next storyline that  last omission however is one of the best  things about Planet Hulk because it  gives us something we rarely see in a  Hulk movie a happy ending  looking at 2017 s Thor Ragnarok through  the eyes of a Hulk fan can feel very  bittersweet on one hand it's the only  live-action adaptation of Planet Hulk  fans are likely to get but on the other  it's tough to know that the closest  we'll get to that story is a film  dedicated to one of the characters  biggest rivals how long have you been  like that like this big green stupid the  hoax dialogue perfectly captures what  any old-school Marvel fans should  remember of the savage Hulk's  monosyllabic speech but in the arena he  winds up having to unwittingly cheat to  win the fight voice activation required  burner  welcome strongest avenger what despite  the contradictions what keeps Ragnarok  so close to the top of this list is the  banter between Hulk and his best  frenemies Thor and all the comedic  moments that go along with it especially  the Hulk's dogged determination to take  down Serdar at the end and as a Hulk  film it's far from perfect but it's  still pretty great infinity war gave us  a lot of Banner and very little Hulk but  2019 Avengers end game rewards fans with  a lot of both by showing us a banner who  treating the Hulk like a disease and  used his genius to merge his mind with  the other guy's body we get to enjoy his  embarrassment at the earlier hulks  caveman persona and once the heroes  gathered the Infinity stones only Hulk  has the power to undo Santos's purge and  survive the ordeal we even get a tribute  to his classic Secret Wars feat of  holding a mountain range at bay  unfortunately the Hulk never gets  another shot at that us in fact he  doesn't get much time in the final  battle at all it's a pretty crowded  scene already sure but after their first  battle ended in such a crushing defeat  you really want to see as much smashing  as possible it's a little ironic that  2012's Avengers is above and beyond all  other Hulk movies not only is his name  not even in the title but he actually  isn't in it all that much the screen  time was limited to the film's two big  action sequences but that was enough for  him to completely steal the show and  provide him with a line that's every bit  as iconic as the classic don't make me  angry that's my secret  I'm always angry that moment marks the  final cohesion of the team and makes him  the movie's most crowd-pleasing star his  hilarious Sucker Punch on Thor in Grand  Central Station  the epic thrashing of Loki in stark  tower in the unique way that he helps  bring Tony Stark back to life are all  pure gamma-powered gold for the first  time Hulk's raw power on the screen  finally mirrors what we've seen in the  comics and the visual effects were never  more impressive before what we saw here  with the Hulk's face actually looking  like a green pumped up version of the  actor playing Bruce Banner just like an  English film we're made to wait quite a  bit to finally see the Hulk emerge the  build-up is perfect and there's enough  room in the movie for him to shine in  the time given unless the impossible  happens and Mark Ruffalo gets his own  solo Hulk flick the green Goliath is  unlikely to get a better portrayal than  what we saw in Avengers check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  superheroes are coming soon subscribe to  our YouTube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

